WEBVTT

00:18.220 --> 00:19.240
Yuko...

00:19.240 --> 00:23.000
Yu-kun, I want you to know.

02:29.920 --> 02:31.830
You're really good, like I remember.

02:31.830 --> 02:32.980
Don't look at it.

02:32.980 --> 02:34.180
Sheesh, you're stingy.

02:34.180 --> 02:36.440
It's not like it'll last longer if I look away.

02:36.440 --> 02:38.960
You're just going to keep on talking if I let you look.

02:38.960 --> 02:43.090
That unfriendliness of yours is why you don't have a girlfriend, you know.

02:43.090 --> 02:45.000
Mind your own business.

02:45.000 --> 02:48.010
Well, now that you have me, everything's fine, right?

02:51.100 --> 02:53.720
So you've started drawing again.

02:53.950 --> 02:55.460
I'm just taking a breather.

02:55.490 --> 02:58.480
Spending all my time studying would actually decrease my efficiency.

02:58.480 --> 03:01.120
So you rationalize everything?

03:01.120 --> 03:03.880
Just as I'd expect of an honor student. You're good at ad-libbing, too.

03:03.880 --> 03:06.290
Hey, you're making fun of me, aren't you?

03:06.290 --> 03:08.720
Nope, I love you.

03:08.720 --> 03:11.690
You're so frivolous with words, like always.

03:11.690 --> 03:14.080
It's just that <i>you're not taking it seriously, Senpai.</i>

03:14.080 --> 03:16.660
I really like you, Himura-senpai.

03:16.660 --> 03:22.130
As long as I get to see your face like this, I feel like I can do my best to live through these days.

03:23.430 --> 03:25.380
You haven't been getting enough sleep, have you?

03:25.380 --> 03:26.540
Sometimes.

03:26.540 --> 03:28.880
Keep that to a minimum, all right?

03:29.980 --> 03:31.610
It's not a laughing matter.

03:31.610 --> 03:33.280
Are you actually studying like you're supposed to?

03:33.280 --> 03:35.100
Good night...

03:43.900 --> 03:45.230
Again?

03:43.900 --> 03:45.230
Art Room

03:43.900 --> 03:45.230
Hirono

03:45.230 --> 03:46.240
Hey, Nagi!

03:46.530 --> 03:47.490
Writing on desks is...

03:47.490 --> 03:49.240
I can't do it anymore.

03:49.240 --> 03:50.200
Huh?

03:50.200 --> 03:52.190
I can't draw anymore.

03:52.190 --> 03:53.490
Nagi?

03:53.490 --> 03:55.730
Even if I do, the drawing gets distorted.

03:55.730 --> 03:58.350
It turns into something I didn't draw.

03:58.350 --> 04:00.540
I keep on drawing over and over again.

04:00.540 --> 04:02.770
But the result turns out the same, without exception.

04:02.770 --> 04:10.910
Little by little, I get confused about whether the picture is distorted, or the artist, or the world.

04:10.910 --> 04:14.490
I'm starting to get nauseous just from picking up a paintbrush.

04:14.490 --> 04:16.700
Maybe you're having what they call an artistic slump?

04:16.700 --> 04:20.490
"It's not a phenomenon that can be defined by a common term like that."

04:20.490 --> 04:21.780
That's what she said.

04:21.780 --> 04:22.890
Who said that?

04:22.890 --> 04:24.940
Me, as the painter.

04:24.940 --> 04:29.410
She's warning me that if this keeps up, I might be unable to ever draw again.

04:29.410 --> 04:31.670
You're giving yourself a warning?

04:31.670 --> 04:34.710
The one giving the warning is me, as a painter.

04:34.710 --> 04:36.120
The one who's hearing it is...

04:38.000 --> 04:39.080
Please leave.

04:39.080 --> 04:40.210
Huh?

04:40.210 --> 04:42.000
Just leave!

04:47.950 --> 04:52.510
The one who's hearing it is... me, as a woman.

04:55.260 --> 04:56.640
Yo, Himura!

04:56.640 --> 04:58.680
You're fine for tomorrow, right?

04:58.680 --> 04:59.540
Tomorrow?

04:59.540 --> 05:01.360
My farewell party.

05:01.360 --> 05:03.190
Ah, I forgot.

05:03.190 --> 05:04.740
You sure are cold.

05:04.740 --> 05:06.830
And you still consider yourself my best friend?

05:06.830 --> 05:07.840
My bad.

05:07.840 --> 05:09.360
Well, I guess it can't be helped.

05:09.490 --> 05:11.400
You have a lot of other things to worry about, don't you?

05:14.320 --> 05:18.660
I guess keeping quiet leaves a bad taste in my mouth.

05:18.660 --> 05:19.910
What is it?

05:19.910 --> 05:22.630
You made me research Yuko-chan, right?

05:22.630 --> 05:23.640
Yeah.

05:23.640 --> 05:27.540
I heard a story from the girls in her class.

05:27.940 --> 05:34.300
According to them, they sometimes get the chills when they look into Amamiya-san's eyes.

05:34.300 --> 05:38.860
Perhaps those girls are the ones who are frightened.

05:38.860 --> 05:41.060
I'm sure you've felt it as well.

05:41.470 --> 05:43.640
Yuko-chan seems a bit of a fraud.

05:43.640 --> 05:47.060
Don't you think she's hiding something?

05:47.060 --> 05:51.320
You're probably the only one who can ask her.

05:59.490 --> 06:00.490
Senpai...

06:00.990 --> 06:03.160
Do you believe in God?

06:03.160 --> 06:08.960
Even if there really was a presence like God once, he's probably not here anymore.

06:08.960 --> 06:09.800
Huh?

06:09.800 --> 06:13.410
The world is full of people who detest fate.

06:13.410 --> 06:15.880
People like that probably killed Him a long time ago.

06:15.880 --> 06:17.170
You're probably right.

06:17.170 --> 06:21.810
If He really did exist, I might have a complaint or two for Him.

06:21.810 --> 06:23.810
Even <i>you get angry?</i>

06:23.810 --> 06:26.710
I don't always wear a nice face, you know.

06:26.710 --> 06:29.600
Everyone has multiple faces.

06:29.600 --> 06:30.420
Faces?

06:30.420 --> 06:33.820
Yes. It might be better to call them masks.

06:33.820 --> 06:37.450
Are you hiding something with that mask as well?

06:37.450 --> 06:39.450
Yes. Of course.

06:41.200 --> 06:44.290
Girls are full of secrets, you know.

06:46.540 --> 06:49.610
Would you like to know my secret?

06:49.610 --> 06:52.310
Just as I thought, you're hiding something, aren't you?

06:52.310 --> 06:55.430
If it's just you, I'll show you, Himura-senpai.

06:55.430 --> 06:56.400
No.

06:56.400 --> 06:58.550
I <i>want you to see it.</i>

06:58.550 --> 07:00.800
The true me.

07:08.130 --> 07:10.940
I agree with you too, Senpai.

07:13.190 --> 07:15.840
Something like God doesn't exist anywhere.

07:15.840 --> 07:20.170
Because there is no God, many sad and painful things occur.

07:20.170 --> 07:24.300
If there really was a God, then I'd want him to make this world more beautiful.

07:24.300 --> 07:30.080
A world where there's no hardship, where everyone is kind, and no one is left alone.

07:30.080 --> 07:33.590
A fairytale world like that doesn't exist anywhere.

07:33.590 --> 07:34.740
I know.

07:34.740 --> 07:37.600
Which is why I want a world like that.

07:53.110 --> 07:55.490
I'm still alive today too.

07:56.420 --> 07:59.020
I'm serious.

07:59.020 --> 08:00.600
I don't mind showing you.

08:00.600 --> 08:01.520
No.

08:01.520 --> 08:02.910
I want to show you.

08:02.910 --> 08:03.870
Just you, Yu-kun.

08:07.870 --> 08:11.080
So you were still here, Nagi?

08:11.470 --> 08:13.090
Hey, Yu.

08:13.090 --> 08:15.710
Kuze's farewell party is going to begin soon.

08:15.710 --> 08:17.960
I just thought of something.

08:19.100 --> 08:24.130
Yu, if we combine Yu and Nagi, it spells "evening calm", doesn't it?

08:24.130 --> 08:25.870
What's this, all of a sudden?

08:25.870 --> 08:29.500
The evening calm is the time when the wind doesn't blow.

08:29.500 --> 08:32.150
With no land or sea breeze,

08:32.150 --> 08:34.740
the air just drifts.

08:34.740 --> 08:37.000
But as time passes,

08:37.000 --> 08:40.220
the wind starts to blow again.

08:40.220 --> 08:42.490
Are you still unable to draw?

08:42.490 --> 08:45.050
Yeah... I forgot.

08:45.050 --> 08:47.330
I'm unable to draw, aren't I?

08:47.640 --> 08:49.330
You're talking as if it's someone else's business.

08:49.330 --> 08:51.580
It's because I know the cause.

08:52.260 --> 08:55.090
Then hurry and resolve it!

08:55.090 --> 08:57.840
You don't have any other redeeming qualities besides the ability to draw.

08:57.840 --> 09:00.840
If that's all there is to the springtime of my youth, it would be a bit lonely.

09:00.840 --> 09:02.220
Nagi...

09:02.220 --> 09:05.350
Yeah. I was lonely.

09:05.350 --> 09:08.220
Since both Kuze and you are drifting away from me.

09:08.520 --> 09:10.480
<i>I'm not going anywhere.</i>

09:10.480 --> 09:12.480
Are you serious when you say that?

09:13.760 --> 09:16.030
You miss the point, as usual.

09:16.030 --> 09:18.730
Or perhaps, you're pretending to miss the point?

09:20.190 --> 09:21.570
I see.

09:21.570 --> 09:24.740
I guess <i>I was the one who missed the point,</i>

09:24.740 --> 09:27.700
since I didn't even notice my own feelings.

09:27.700 --> 09:29.040
Nagi?

09:29.040 --> 09:32.940
I thought this moment in time would last forever.

09:32.940 --> 09:35.790
Even though that could never be true.

09:35.790 --> 09:37.920
I guess I was too late to notice.

09:37.920 --> 09:39.920
I'm sorry, Nagi...

09:39.920 --> 09:41.300
Don't apologize to me!

09:42.920 --> 09:47.180
I guess I couldn't draw because I couldn't see the true me.

09:47.550 --> 09:50.310
I might be able to draw now.

09:50.310 --> 09:51.780
Please go.

09:51.780 --> 09:53.490
Isn't Yuko-chan waiting for you?

09:59.130 --> 10:02.360
What, are we the only people you managed to gather?

10:02.360 --> 10:06.540
Nope, I only planned to invite you two from the very beginning.

10:06.540 --> 10:09.240
What's going to happen now isn't really a farewell party,

10:09.240 --> 10:12.500
but more of a performance by Kuze Shuichi.

10:12.500 --> 10:14.000
A performance?

10:14.000 --> 10:17.070
I've never let you hear me play before, have I?

10:17.070 --> 10:21.000
I'm going to give this to you as a parting present, so listen to it gratefully.

10:21.000 --> 10:25.380
Oh? You sound as if you're going to play it only for Himura-senpai.

10:25.380 --> 10:27.070
Ah, pardon me.

10:27.070 --> 10:32.520
Today, for my two beloved friends, Himura Yu and Amamiya Yuko,

10:33.520 --> 10:37.770
I'm going to give my last and best performance in this country.

10:38.040 --> 10:40.770
In this place that's filled with memories.

11:25.190 --> 11:26.950
Yuko?

11:29.660 --> 11:31.030
Yuko!

11:34.040 --> 11:37.540
On my way home with a smile on my face

11:34.040 --> 11:37.540
looking for my voice that I have lost

11:41.790 --> 11:44.800
I'm sorry, Himura-senpai.

11:49.510 --> 11:51.220
I cried by accident.

11:51.220 --> 11:53.470
To play so beautifully,

11:53.760 --> 11:57.980
Kuze-senpai must have an honest and pure heart.

11:58.850 --> 12:03.290
It was truly beautiful, a sound both serene and undistorted.

12:03.290 --> 12:07.550
Kuze-senpai must've grown up being loved by everyone around him.

12:07.550 --> 12:10.480
And that's why he can produce such beauty.

12:10.480 --> 12:14.530
It was so beautiful that I couldn't bear to hear it.

12:14.530 --> 12:18.180
"Perhaps there is some worth in this world."

12:18.180 --> 12:22.130
I couldn't believe I was actually thinking that myself.

12:22.130 --> 12:23.790
Why couldn't you just believe it?

12:25.380 --> 12:29.260
Why can't you just accept what you felt?

12:29.260 --> 12:30.760
Senpai...

12:30.760 --> 12:35.010
Or do you truly believe there is no worth in this world?

12:35.010 --> 12:38.390
Yuko, what are you holding back?

12:38.390 --> 12:39.890
Nothing in particular.

12:39.890 --> 12:40.890
That's a lie!

12:40.890 --> 12:42.440
It isn't.

12:42.440 --> 12:43.810
No, it's a lie.

12:44.240 --> 12:47.650
You don't say what you want to say,
and you don't ask what you want to ask.

12:47.650 --> 12:50.030
When someone asks you a question, you don't answer.

12:50.030 --> 12:52.950
All you do is fend it off with silence or nonsense.

12:53.240 --> 12:56.790
Where does the truth end, and the lie begin?

12:56.790 --> 12:59.200
When you say you love me, which is it?

13:00.710 --> 13:03.080
Is it true, or is it a lie?

13:15.000 --> 13:17.260
Yuko, please tell me.

13:17.260 --> 13:19.150
Tell you... what?

13:19.150 --> 13:20.830
Don't evade the question!

13:20.830 --> 13:22.740
I want an answer!

13:22.740 --> 13:24.930
You're arrogant, aren't you, Senpai?

13:24.930 --> 13:26.150
I don't care if I'm arrogant.

13:26.150 --> 13:27.470
Please tell me.

13:27.470 --> 13:29.820
Why are you being so stubborn?

13:29.820 --> 13:32.450
Because I love you!

13:33.370 --> 13:35.950
That's why I want to know about you!

13:36.700 --> 13:39.080
Is that true?

13:39.080 --> 13:40.200
Yeah.

13:40.200 --> 13:43.580
Do you really love me?

13:43.580 --> 13:44.710
Yeah.

13:44.710 --> 13:48.210
Do you really want to know about me?

13:48.210 --> 13:49.250
Yeah.

13:49.250 --> 13:50.450
Then...

13:50.450 --> 13:53.600
will you really, really listen to my story?

13:53.630 --> 13:55.140
Yeah.

13:58.230 --> 14:01.170
You... finally said it.

14:01.170 --> 14:04.580
I wanted to make you say it.

14:04.580 --> 14:08.650
I needed you to want me...

14:13.650 --> 14:15.770
Please let me ask you one thing.

14:15.770 --> 14:16.760
Sure.

14:16.760 --> 14:21.750
When I was at the orphanage, I was always chasing you.

14:21.750 --> 14:24.080
I watched you every day.

14:24.080 --> 14:25.190
You're right.

14:25.190 --> 14:30.170
But despite that, why didn't you become my older brother?

14:31.000 --> 14:34.420
If you'd become my older brother, I could've...

14:34.420 --> 14:35.680
I could've...

14:35.900 --> 14:38.430
stayed beautiful.

14:40.510 --> 14:43.710
Yu-kun, I want you to know...

14:43.710 --> 14:46.190
how I really look.

14:47.940 --> 14:50.920
I wonder where and how I messed up.

14:50.920 --> 14:54.620
I'm always thinking about it,
but I still don't know the answer.

14:54.620 --> 14:58.490
Or perhaps, it's this world that's messed up?

14:58.490 --> 15:00.410
Nii-san was nice.

15:00.720 --> 15:03.950
He took me out to play, and he helped me with my studies.

15:03.950 --> 15:07.200
He was nice to me, as if we were true siblings.

15:07.200 --> 15:12.930
But, as his time with me kept accumulating, he must've realized...

15:12.930 --> 15:16.810
that I wasn't his real sister.

15:16.810 --> 15:21.830
Nii-san was trying to substitute me for his sister, who died in the earthquake.

15:21.830 --> 15:24.660
But I was a different person.

15:24.660 --> 15:27.090
His sister was no longer there.

15:27.090 --> 15:29.230
The person with him was just a stranger.

15:29.230 --> 15:34.260
When he realized that, he came to detest me.

15:34.260 --> 15:40.260
Ever since he lost his sister, intense anger had been swirling inside his heart,

15:40.260 --> 15:44.050
and he was looking for someone to vent his fury on.

15:44.050 --> 15:46.240
And that's when I appeared.

15:46.240 --> 15:49.770
At first, he just hit me and threw things at me.

15:49.770 --> 15:52.880
But you know, he even treated my injuries,

15:52.880 --> 15:55.570
and he apologized many times.

15:55.570 --> 16:00.010
But two years ago, during that Christmas, he...

16:01.010 --> 16:04.530
You know, I had my first experience during that Christmas.

16:04.530 --> 16:06.140
He was thoughtful, wasn't he?

16:07.140 --> 16:10.710
I really wanted to give my virginity to the one I loved.

16:10.710 --> 16:15.150
I wanted my first time to be gentle and affectionate, and to be treated like a princess.

16:15.150 --> 16:18.300
My dream was shattered into pieces in a heartbeat.

16:18.300 --> 16:21.040
I was dressed nicely, you know, because it was Christmas.

16:21.040 --> 16:23.080
I still had hopes.

16:23.080 --> 16:26.790
I wanted my brother to praise me for dressing so cutely.

16:26.790 --> 16:31.260
But after he hit me like usual, I fell, and my skirt flipped up.

16:31.260 --> 16:34.420
When I tried to pull my skirt back down,
he grasped my hands, and...

16:34.420 --> 16:35.590
Stop it...

16:35.590 --> 16:37.760
They were such cute clothes, too.

16:37.760 --> 16:38.880
Stop it...

16:38.880 --> 16:41.300
When I tried to resist, he hit me again.

16:41.300 --> 16:42.550
Stop it!

16:42.550 --> 16:44.680
He wouldn't stop even though I was crying.

16:44.680 --> 16:46.060
Stop it!

16:46.060 --> 16:50.440
In just one night, my body became unfit for marriage.

16:50.440 --> 16:52.900
Stop it!

16:54.690 --> 16:58.220
If you'd been my first, it would've been wonderful, Senpai.

16:58.220 --> 17:03.230
If it had been you, you'd have done it gently, like that kiss.

17:03.230 --> 17:05.450
It's unfortunate. Very unfortunate.

17:06.170 --> 17:09.020
I don't have anything left anymore.

17:09.020 --> 17:12.060
Neither a past that I can treasure, nor a future with any dreams.

17:12.060 --> 17:15.670
I'm a tool to be used for anger and hate.

17:15.670 --> 17:18.840
I'm a doll, that can't even substitute for the dead.

17:18.840 --> 17:20.000
No!

17:20.000 --> 17:22.720
You're neither a tool nor a doll!

17:23.510 --> 17:25.190
Don't say you don't have a future!

17:25.190 --> 17:27.390
As long as you're alive, there can be some happiness too!

17:28.180 --> 17:31.560
No matter how painful the past is, it's possible to forget it!

17:32.350 --> 17:35.980
As long as you keep on believing,
it's even possible to change the future!

17:36.770 --> 17:39.900
So... don't say that you don't have a future!

17:40.940 --> 17:43.400
You really are simple-minded, aren't you?

17:44.070 --> 17:45.450
This is from yesterday.

17:45.450 --> 17:46.840
This is from the day before yesterday.

17:46.840 --> 17:50.260
This was inflicted above the place that had almost healed over last week.

17:50.260 --> 17:53.260
Maybe around the time that you were at home studying?

17:53.260 --> 17:57.810
Yes. Even after I met you, it's been going on every night.

17:57.810 --> 17:59.110
For a long time...

17:59.110 --> 18:02.630
No, it may have gotten worse since I met you.

18:02.630 --> 18:05.020
This is from the night after we were reunited.

18:05.020 --> 18:08.210
This is from the night after you and Nagi-san went shopping.

18:08.210 --> 18:11.340
This is from the night after I called you out on the rooftop.

18:11.340 --> 18:14.420
This is from the night after you went and found my slippers for me.

18:14.420 --> 18:17.860
This is from the night after we went out on a date to buy shoes.

18:17.860 --> 18:20.730
If I show even a hint of unwillingness, he's severe.

18:20.730 --> 18:24.660
If I try to avoid that by pretending to be obedient, he's more violent.

18:24.660 --> 18:30.250
I wondered over and over whether I did something bad... something that deserves punishment like this,

18:30.250 --> 18:32.820
but I couldn't think of anything,

18:32.820 --> 18:36.150
and eventually, I started not to care anymore.

18:36.150 --> 18:42.130
And now, I've become someone who is waiting for the day that I will disappear and be gone.

18:42.130 --> 18:45.750
But... the days I have remaining are very harsh.

18:46.610 --> 18:49.100
It hurts. It's hot. It's painful.

18:49.100 --> 18:51.430
It's sad. It's harsh. I wanted to cry.

18:51.430 --> 18:54.620
I couldn't stand it. I couldn't run. I couldn't resist.

18:54.620 --> 18:57.200
It wouldn't end. I wanted to turn away. I wanted to scream.

18:57.200 --> 18:59.440
I wanted to fight back. I wanted to throw up. I wanted to end it.

18:59.440 --> 19:02.360
I wanted to resist. I wanted to oppose. I wanted to rebel.

19:02.360 --> 19:04.710
I wanted to run. I wanted to hide. I wanted to avoid it.

19:04.710 --> 19:07.300
I wanted to shut myself in. I wanted to refuse, I wanted to bite him.

19:07.300 --> 19:09.310
I wanted to push him aside. I wanted to shake him off.

19:09.310 --> 19:11.570
I was pursued, I was seized, I was dragged out.

19:11.570 --> 19:13.960
I was attacked, I was forced, I was not forgiven,

19:13.960 --> 19:16.650
I was restrained, I was bound, I was pushed,

19:16.650 --> 19:19.290
I was torn apart, I was thrown, I was treated cruelly,

19:19.290 --> 19:21.000
I wanted to groan, I wanted to scream, I wanted to go crazy,

19:21.000 --> 19:22.300
I couldn't bear it.

19:22.300 --> 19:24.090
I was grabbed, I was hit, I was torn,

19:24.090 --> 19:25.640
I was crushed, I was cut, I was burned,

19:25.640 --> 19:27.170
I was stabbed, I was burned some more, I was defiled,

19:27.170 --> 19:28.880
I was ripped apart, I was ruined, I was destroyed,

19:28.880 --> 19:30.790
I was mocked, I was toyed with, I was crushed.

19:30.790 --> 19:33.100
I was trampled, he got tired of me, I was thrown out.

19:33.100 --> 19:36.190
I was torn up, and he threw me away. I fainted, my pain went numb,

19:36.190 --> 19:39.810
my heart was broken, I couldn't cry. But I was picked up again, and

19:39.810 --> 19:42.450
I was grabbed again, I was hit again, I was defiled again.

19:42.450 --> 19:45.020
I was torn again, I was crushed again, I was cut again,

19:45.020 --> 19:48.490
I was stabbed again, I was burned again.

19:51.370 --> 19:52.520
Even though I hate it.

19:52.520 --> 20:03.020
Even though I hate it, even though I hate it...

20:12.960 --> 20:17.270
This is the true me, the one you didn't know.

20:17.270 --> 20:22.020
This is the girl you abandoned.

20:17.430 --> 20:22.020
This is the girl
1you abandoned.

20:32.790 --> 20:41.880
tooi hi no yume oikakete

20:32.790 --> 20:41.880
I chase after the dreams of a distant day

20:43.470 --> 20:52.600
asa no hikari ni kieteyuku

20:43.470 --> 20:52.600
and disappear into the morning light.

20:54.140 --> 21:03.530
kurikaesu hibi no naka

20:54.140 --> 21:03.530
Within the days that repeat themselves

21:04.490 --> 21:14.250
utsurou kisetsu ga tookute

21:04.490 --> 21:14.250
the changing seasons seem so far away.

21:18.210 --> 21:27.470
kanawanai negai nara

21:18.210 --> 21:27.470
If it is a wish that cannot be granted

21:28.800 --> 21:35.230
kizukanai furi shite

21:28.800 --> 21:35.230
I pretend that I don't notice

21:36.850 --> 21:40.860
warau

21:36.850 --> 21:40.860
and smile.

21:59.670 --> 22:02.630
Senpai, do you remember that day?

22:02.630 --> 22:03.670
That day?

22:03.840 --> 22:05.670
I asked you, didn't I?

22:06.630 --> 22:09.050
"Don't you want a sister?"

22:10.050 --> 22:15.640
I found a distant relative that was willing to take me in.

22:15.640 --> 22:19.560
But they said they'd respect my wishes about what I wanted to do.

22:20.560 --> 22:25.190
At that time, you were the only person I could open my heart to.

22:25.190 --> 22:29.450
If you'd said that you wanted a sister, then I...

22:30.450 --> 22:33.280
But you shook off my hand.

22:34.330 --> 22:37.370
Why couldn't you have said that you wanted a sister?

22:38.370 --> 22:40.830
Why couldn't you have told me not to go?

22:41.880 --> 22:44.460
Why couldn't you have told me to stay?

22:45.460 --> 22:48.130
Why couldn't you have protected me?

22:49.130 --> 22:50.260
Why not?

22:51.140 --> 22:54.180
I didn't want to make you a substitute for her.

22:54.180 --> 22:58.520
I didn't want... to make you a substitute for Akane, who'd died!

22:59.390 --> 23:01.270
Liar.

23:05.900 --> 23:07.650
Did you know, Senpai?

23:07.650 --> 23:12.530
You have a habit of blinking a lot when you tell a lie.

23:12.530 --> 23:16.200
But you told me that you loved me

23:16.200 --> 23:17.700
without blinking.

23:19.210 --> 23:22.250
But you're ten years too late.

23:25.210 --> 23:27.800
What rises against everything, is courage.

23:27.880 --> 23:29.340
Or perhaps...

23:29.840 --> 23:33.090
ef - a tale of melodies.

23:33.220 --> 23:34.680
Reflection.

23:35.100 --> 23:38.560
Can you hear it? The melody of truth.
